            the corpus's `type:` vocabulary preserves the kind-
            distinction while the substrate routes both to one class).
            Example: :mm/Tag declares `:dt/codec-type-keyword :tag` so
            files with `type: tag` parse as :mm/Tag entities (not
            :mm/Memory with memory-type :tag).  Default routing target
            (when no class claims the type-keyword) is :mm/Memory.
