            paired with the canonical namespaced slot ident.  Codecs
            read this via `sandbar.db.datatype/codec-aliases-of` for
            class-declared alias resolution.

            NOTE — these are NOT owl:sameAs-shaped identity aliases.
            They are context-specific naming conventions for the codec
            layer ONLY: when a class is encoded via a codec, short-key
            surfaces in the wire form as a stand-in for the canonical
            namespaced slot.  The slot retains its full canonical
            identity in the model; only the wire-form name is short.

            Attribute name `:dt/codec-aliases` (not `:dt/aliases`)
            chosen to disambiguate from OWL identity-relation
            semantics + to match the `:dt/native-codec` sister
            attribute naming pattern, per
            interaction/check_substrate_schema_attribute_names_against_rdf_owl_semantics_2026_05_13.md.

            Example: on :mm/Memory, [:type :mm.memory/memory-type]
            tells the markdown codec that frontmatter key `type:` maps
            to slot :mm.memory/memory-type (avoiding collision with
            the :dt/type system attribute).

            Replaces the prior hardcoded `known-class-slot-aliases`
            map in `sandbar.codec.markdown` per
            interaction/no_hardcoded_consumer_class_knowledge_in_substrate_2026_05_13.md
            + decisions/sandbar_dt_star_explicit_ident_entity_helper_split_2026_05_13.md."}

  {:db/ident :dt/codec-slot-order
   :dt/type  :dt/Property
   :dt/domain :dt/Class
   :dt/range :db.type/tuple
   :db/valueType :db.type/tuple
   :db/tupleTypes [:db.type/keyword :db.type/long]
   :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
   :db/doc "Per-class CANONICAL slot ordering for codec emit.  Each
            entry is `[slot-ident position]` — a heterogeneous tuple
            pairing the canonical namespaced slot ident with its
            sort position (smaller = earlier).  Codecs read this via
            `sandbar.db.datatype/codec-slot-order-of` to introspect
            the class-declared emit order.

            Distinct from `:dt/slots` — `:dt/slots` is the cardinality-
            many SET of slots belonging to a class (membership, order
            lost at transact); `:dt/codec-slot-order` is the ORDERED
            sequence specifically governing wire-form emit.  The two
            CAN diverge: slots that exist on a class but never surface
            in the wire form (e.g., :mm.memory/body-raw, structural-
            graph slots) MAY be omitted from `:dt/codec-slot-order`.

            Codec semantics:
              - On emit, the codec introspects this attribute and
                writes slots in the declared order.  Slots present in
                the entity but absent from the ordering are appended
                at the end (in entity-key iteration order).
              - On parse, this attribute has NO effect — parse just
                accumulates whatever the source provides.  Round-trip
                fidelity for slot-ordering comes from emit producing
                CANONICAL class-declared order, not from preserving
                source-text accident.

            Per decisions/slot_order_declared_by_class_introspectable_2026_05_20.md
            (Dan-directive 2026-05-20: 'slot order should be declared
            by the class and introspectable').  Replaces the prior
            `:codec/key-order` metadata threading pattern that carried
            source-text order through parse → entity → emit (brittle:
            metadata dropped on any new map construction)."}

  {:db/ident :dt/bm25f-weights
   :dt/type  :dt/Property
   :dt/domain :dt/Class
   :dt/range :db.type/tuple
   :db/valueType :db.type/tuple
   :db/tupleTypes [:db.type/keyword :db.type/double]
   :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
   :db/doc "Per-class default BM25F field-weights for fulltext search.
            Each entry is [slot-ident weight] — a heterogeneous tuple
            pairing the canonical namespaced slot ident with its
            multi-field BM25F scoring weight.  Consumed by
            sandbar.search/search-bm25f when no :field-weights opt is
            provided on the query; a per-query :field-weights opt
            overrides.

            Algorithm-specific name (`bm25f-weights`) chosen over a
            bare `weights` to disambiguate from any RDF/OWL weighted-
            axiom semantics, per
            interaction/check_substrate_schema_attribute_names_against_rdf_owl_semantics_2026_05_13.md.

            Heterogeneous tuple shape ([keyword double]) declared via
            :db/tupleTypes (plural) — Datomic's fixed-length typed-pair
            form, distinct from :db/tupleType (singular, homogeneous).
            Sister attribute :dt/codec-aliases uses the homogeneous
            form (two keywords); :dt/bm25f-weights mixes keyword +
            double so requires the plural form.

            Example: on :mm/Memory,
              [[:mm.memory/name 12.0]
               [:mm.memory/description 8.0]
               [:mm.memory/body-raw 1.0]]
            tells sandbar.search/search-bm25f to weight name-matches
            12x, description-matches 8x, and body-matches 1x when
            scoring fulltext hits against the memory class.

            Per fulltext arc Stage 1 of
            plans/sandbar_fulltext_search_substrate_arc_2026_05_13.md."}

  {:db/ident :dt/memorial-policy
   :dt/type  :dt/Property
   :dt/domain :dt/Class
   :dt/range :db.type/keyword
   :db/valueType :db.type/keyword
   :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
   :db/doc "Per-class declarative classification governing how instances
            are persisted + projected to the fs corpus.  Three values:

              :first-class — instances project to memory/<class-path>/<ident>.md
                             via the reactive sink (sandbar.reactive.sinks);
                             BM25F-searchable + human-editable + git-versioned

              :db-only     — instances stay DB-resident; covered by the DB-dump
                             arc for disaster recovery + audit

              :inline      — instances serialize inline within host memorials
                             (e.g., :mm/Tag in :mm.memory/tags)

            The reactive-projection sink consults this slot at projection time
            to decide whether to materialize a fs counterpart.  The DB-dump arc
            consults this slot at dump time to decide whether to include.

            Per decisions/option_b_plus_c_ratified_spec_vs_state_criterion_pivot_to_first_class_memorialization_2026_05_23.md
            + plans/sandbar_first_class_memorialization_arc_workflows_schedules_contexts_dt_memorial_policy_2026_05_23.md
