;; Property-Characteristic Marker Classes (OWL 2 RL aligned)
;;
;; Each marker class is a sub-class of :dt/Property.  A predicate slot declares
;; its property-characteristics by adding `:dt/type :dt/<MarkerClass>` to its
;; slot definition (cardinality-many `:dt/type` permits multiple markers per
;; property — e.g. an asymmetric+irreflexive predicate).
;;
;; Names align with OWL 2 RL `prp-*` rule families per
;; resources/w3c_owl2_rl_in_rif_2012.md — entailment rules at the substrate
;; layer (Layer 0 per plans/layered_rule_subsystem_architecture_arc_2026_05_21.md)
;; can compile from these marker-class assertions to native Datomic Datalog
;; rules.
;;
;; Per interaction/check_substrate_schema_attribute_names_against_rdf_owl_semantics_2026_05_13.md
;; the names follow OWL 2 canonical terminology exactly.
