   :dt/slots []
   :dt/label "Asymmetric Property"
   :db/doc "OWL 2 owl:AsymmetricProperty alignment.  A property whose extension is asymmetric: (?p type AsymmetricProperty) ∧ (x p y) → ¬(y p x).  Compiles to OWL 2 RL rule prp-asyp (consistency check; firing implies inconsistency).  Logically: asymmetric ≡ antisymmetric + irreflexive — see :dt/AntisymmetricProperty for the weaker variant the corpus uses for mereology (has-part / part-of)."}

  {:db/ident :dt/AntisymmetricProperty
   :dt/type :dt/Class
   :dt/subclass-of :dt/Property
   :dt/context "meta"
   :dt/slots []
   :dt/label "Antisymmetric Property"
   :db/doc "Antisymmetric property characteristic — used by the corpus for proper-mereology predicates (has-part / part-of).  Antisymmetric ≡ ∀x∀y. (x R y ∧ y R x → x = y); weaker than asymmetric (which is antisymmetric + irreflexive).  NOT an OWL 2 standard characteristic (OWL has only owl:AsymmetricProperty); declared here because the corpus's predicate memorials distinguish — has-part / part-of use `antisymmetric` (allowing in principle x = y self-relations, though irreflexive is also declared making the practical effect equivalent to asymmetric).  When compiling to OWL 2 RL rules, treat antisymmetric + irreflexive declarations as if asymmetric (both compile to prp-asyp consistency check)."}

  {:db/ident :dt/ReflexiveProperty
